From d7d8783a0ca39208aac2536cb01282f50a888220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:53:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Perf][ROCm] MoE int4 interleave unpacking for GPTQ/AWQ
 Triton kernel (#43389)

Adapted for FLASHNEXT_VLLM_REF=2a4cd640 (vllm#53896 head). Upstream PR #43389
(open, under review as of 2026-08-28) against vllm main; verified
git apply --check clean on the 2a4cd640 tree (core vllm/ files only --
tests/kernels/moe/test_moe.py and benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_moe.py are
excluded since they conflict against this older tree and are not needed at
runtime).

Optimizes the MoE int4 Triton kernel (fused_moe_kernel_gptq_awq) on ROCm by
repacking weights at load time from K-packed [E, N, K//2] uint8 to N-packed
[E, K, N//8] int32, then unpacking in-kernel via tl.interleave with constant
GPTQ sequential shifts, instead of loading each packed int4 byte twice (once
per nibble) with per-element variable shifts. Zero points are unpacked to
fp16 at load time too. Gated behind on_rdna() (vllm/platforms/rocm.py) and
num_bits==4, so it activates for our gfx1201 (RDNA4) W4A16 MoE path
(CompressedTensorsWNA16MoEMethod -> convert_to_wna16_moe_kernel_format,
same oracle/int_wna16.py dispatch our boot log shows as
'Using TRITON WNA16 MoE backend') without touching CDNA/Instinct.

Author (amd-xavierwang, AMD) posted gsm8k full-dataset accuracy validation
on gfx1100/gfx1151/gfx1201 in PR comments showing no regression at time of
writing; PR is still open pending reviewer sign-off on broader-arch safety
(dllehr-amd asked about gfx9/Instinct; author responded by gating to
on_rdna() only, i.e. RDNA family, CDNA unaffected). We carry this as a local
patch to get the perf win now rather than wait for merge+release; drop this
patch once #43389 lands in an FLASHNEXT_VLLM_REF bump.

Upstream: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/43389
